    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "A look at the math that OpenAI claims computes faster Fourier transforms",
      "url": "https://www.argmin.net/p/faster-fourier-transforms",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50065932",
      "score": 189,
      "comments": 123,
      "author": "mochomocha",
      "published": "2026-10-13T02:46:43Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Deconstructs OpenAI's theoretical arithmetic reductions against standard O(N log N) Cooley-Tukey algorithms for discrete Fourier transforms.",
        "Crucial for long-context architectures, Mamba-style state-space models, and FlashFFTConv relying on fast convolutions over dense attention.",
        "Practitioners caution that theoretical operation reductions rarely translate to GPU wall-clock speedups without optimizing memory bandwidth and tensor cores."
      ]
    },
